content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-112 - AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22300",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 2.0 mm/s is in Zone A (0.0-2.8 mm/s RMS, 'New machines') of HF-300 Figure 3. This is well below the 7.1 mm/s Zone D limit ('Damage likely - stop the pump'). The SSP-07 stop-immediately rule for the highest severity zone is therefore not triggered. The report does not say whether the value is RMS or the highest of both bearing housings, as section 3 requires.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing housing temperature 65 C is within the manual's 'normal up to 70 C' range. It is below the 80 C alarm and 90 C trip limits. The SSP-07 priority-1 trigger (temperature above the manufacturer's alarm limit) does not apply. The manual's limits are for housing-surface temperature, which matches the reported housing reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Flow has dropped about 20% over two weeks at unchanged valve settings. This is a performance shortfall against the rated duty of 300 m3/h at 45 m. No absolute flow or head reading was given, so the actual operating point cannot be compared with the rating.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage is reported, so the troubleshooting symptom 'Leakage at shaft seal' does not apply. There is no evidence-based reason to replace the seal routinely.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Priority set to P2: no stop or P1 criterion in SSP-07 or the manual is met. A progressive 20% flow loss still needs planned corrective work. The site's P2/P3 definitions are not in the evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn impeller and/or worn wear rings. This fits a gradual flow loss over two weeks at fixed valve settings, with normal vibration and temperature. Corrective action: inspect the impeller and wear rings.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Air in the suction / air in the casing. Corrective action: vent the casing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Closed or partly closed valve, such as a valve that has drifted or a blockage, even though the settings are reported unchanged. Verify the actual valve positions.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Non-intrusive checks with the pump running: confirm that the suction and discharge valves are actually in their recorded open positions.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vent the casing to remove any trapped air. Then re-check flow and record whether it recovers.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Take vibration readings on both bearing housings in mm/s RMS. Classify the highest reading against Figure 3, and record it together with the housing temperature as a baseline.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If flow does not recover, stop the pump and apply electrical LOTO at the MCC. Mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves. Obtain a line-break permit, then drain and vent the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly (68 kg) under a signed lifting plan using certified lifting equipment. The casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01",
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller. Inspect the impeller (HF3-210) and wear rings for wear or damage. Replace the impeller if worn.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Only if the seal is disturbed or found damaged: fit cartridge seal HF3-450B, not HF3-450, because SB-2026-014 applies to serial HF3-22300. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed. Inspect shaft sleeve HF3-455 and replace it if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. Torque the seal gland nuts to 30 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Refit the impeller and torque the impeller nut (M24) to 160 Nm, with lightly oiled threads.",
      "citations": [
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit a new casing gasket HF3-120; this is mandatory whenever the casing is opened. Refit the back pull-out assembly and torque the casing bolts (M16) to 210 Nm. If the bearing housing bolts (M12) were disturbed, torque them to 85 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-align the pump to the motor, since the bearing housing has been moved. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, fill and vent the pump. Never run it dry; the seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the isolations, restart, and confirm flow at the original valve settings. Record vibration against Figure 3 and housing temperature against the 70/80/90 C limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C06"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket - required, replace whenever the casing is opened",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-210",
      "description": "Impeller, 5-vane, 330 mm - fit if inspection shows wear",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal (supersedes HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above) - contingency, fit only if the seal is disturbed or damaged",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve - contingency, replace if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC before any work inside the pump or on its seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Obtain a line-break permit; drain and vent before breaking containment.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, which is over the 25 kg limit. A lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment are required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not run the pump dry on restart; it must be filled and vented first.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the lines are chemically dosed, wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If any vibration reading reaches Zone D (above 7.1 mm/s RMS), stop the pump immediately. Notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Back pull-out removal and impeller access: there is no standard time for impeller inspection or replacement. The closest reference is mechanical seal replacement (same disassembly path), at 4.0 h with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment after reassembly: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Planning estimate is about 5.5 h of elapsed work: 2 technicians for about 4.0 h, plus 1 technician for 1.5 h. This excludes the initial venting and valve checks, which have no standard time.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal part: manual Rev D lists HF3-450 (component seal). SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes it with HF3-450B for HF-300 serial HF3-22000 and above. P-112 is serial HF3-22300, which is in range, so the bulletin applies: do not fit HF3-450.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm (M10). SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. 30 Nm applies to this asset, because its serial (HF3-22300) is at or above HF3-22000.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve inspection: manual 5.2 says inspect the sleeve for scoring with no limit, and implies sleeve measurement for the component seal. The bulletin says HF3-450B is pre-set with no sleeve measurement, and to replace HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm. The bulletin criteria apply to serial HF3-22300.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "All other Table 5 torques (casing bolts 210 Nm, impeller nut 160 Nm, bearing housing bolts 85 Nm) are not changed by the bulletin. They remain applicable.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is the reported 2.0 mm/s an RMS value, and is it the highest of the two bearing-housing readings as section 3 requires?",
    "What were the actual flow and discharge head (or pressure) before and after the drop? No absolute values were given for comparison with the 300 m3/h at 45 m rating.",
    "Wear ring part numbers and wear/clearance limits are not in the parts list or the procedures.",
    "No acceptance criteria are given for impeller wear, so the decision to replace the impeller is left to technician judgement.",
    "There is no standard labour time for impeller or wear ring inspection and replacement in Table 6.",
    "Are P-112's lines chemically dosed? This determines whether chemical PPE is required.",
    "Suction conditions (NPSH available, suction strainer condition, suction pressure) are not reported, so air ingress or suction restriction cannot be confirmed or ruled out from the evidence.",
    "The site's definitions for P2 versus P3 priority are not in the evidence. P2 is a planner judgement.",
    "It is not stated whether the coupling or motor must be disturbed for back pull-out on this installation. Alignment is planned because the bearing housing is moved."
  ]
}
